        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #0E1C42; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 10px;">A few words in this lesson are worth reviewing before you read. They are shown in bold with a dotted line. Hover over one to see what it means.</div>
        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 6px;"><strong>citizen</strong><button type="button" class="gloss-audio" aria-label="Play pronunciation of citizen" onclick="speakGloss(event,'citizen')">&#128266;</button> <span style="color: #6b7a99;">(SIT-ih-zun)</span>: A member of a country or state who has rights and also duties.</div>
        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 6px;"><strong>interest group</strong><button type="button" class="gloss-audio" aria-label="Play pronunciation of interest group" onclick="speakGloss(event,'interest group')">&#128266;</button> <span style="color: #6b7a99;">(IN-ter-est GROOP)</span>: A group of people who work together to influence leaders on an issue they care about.</div>
        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 6px;"><strong>jury</strong><button type="button" class="gloss-audio" aria-label="Play pronunciation of jury" onclick="speakGloss(event,'jury')">&#128266;</button> <span style="color: #6b7a99;">(JOOR-ee)</span>: A group of citizens chosen to listen to a court case and decide the facts.</div>
        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 6px;"><strong>lobby</strong><button type="button" class="gloss-audio" aria-label="Play pronunciation of lobby" onclick="speakGloss(event,'lobby')">&#128266;</button> <span style="color: #6b7a99;">(LOB-ee)</span>: To try to persuade lawmakers to pass or reject a law.</div>
